ethanol, carbon monoxide, methane, hydrogen
sulphide, and acetone) is associated with a variety of
metabolic and pathologic conditions.9-13, 17, 18

Breath analysis continues to be an interesting field
for noninvasively diagnosis of serious illnesses.
Biomarker analysis in breath may be the most simple,
rapid and safest way to accurately determine the
stage or the severity of a dysfunction.36-38 Although
numerous biomarkers have been identified so far,
very little is known about their origin, if they are
metabolic or not.4-6, 36-38
